.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER-BOOTSTRAP 1 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create or refresh the mu2edaq-file-reaper environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
[\fB\-\-extras\fR]
.br
.B MU2EDAQ_PYTHON=\fIpython3.9\fR ./bootstrap.sh
.br
.B powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\bootstrap.ps1
[\fB\-Extras\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates
.I ./venv
when it does not exist, installs the runtime and development dependencies
from
.IR requirements.txt " and " requirements-dev.txt ,
installs the package in editable mode (providing the
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper " and " mu2edaq-reaper
console scripts), and then best-effort installs the two Mu2e libraries that
are not on PyPI:
.B mu2edaq-discovery
and
.BR mu2edaq-notify .
Each is taken from the sibling checkout in
.I mu2edaq-main
when present, otherwise from GitHub; when neither works the reaper runs
without discovery or phone notifications.  Finally the
.IR data/ ", " logs/ " and " config/
directories are created.  Re-running is safe and updates dependencies.
.PP
A failure installing the required dependencies or the package itself stops
the script with a message; the environment is then not usable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-extras
Also install
.B pyzmq
(DAQ message channel) and
.B zstandard
(zstd compression).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the virtual environment (default
.BR python3 ).
On AlmaLinux 9 the system
.B python3
is 3.9, the production target.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when a required install step fails; 2 for an unknown option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-start (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1)
